<given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Crosbie</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Brink</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Kantor</surname><given-names>AB</given-names></name><name><surname>Basten</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodnow</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Elimination from peripheral lymphoid tissues of self-reactive B lymphocytes recognizing membrane-bound antigens</article-title><source>Nature</source><year>1991</year><volume>353</volume><fpage>765</fpage><lpage>769</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1944535</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B10"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Okamoto</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Murakami</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Shimizu</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Ozaki</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Tsubata</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Kumagai</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Honjo</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>A transgenic model of autoimmune hemolytic anemia</article-title><source>J Exp Med</source><year>1992</year><volume>175</volume><fpage>71</fpage><lpage>79</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1730928</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B11"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hartley</surname><given-names>SB</given-names></name><name><surname>Goodnow</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Censoring of self-reactive B cells with a range of receptor affinities in transgenic mice expressing heavy chains for a lysozyme-specific antibody</article-title><source>Int Immunol</source><year>1994</year><volume>6</volu